      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Indus Valley Civilization relied on agrarian surplus, specialized crafts, and flourishing maritime trade with Western Asia.",
        "The Vedic economy transitioned from pastoral nomadic life to settled iron-age agriculture, altering social structure and religious practices.",
        "The Mauryan Empire featured state-monopolized industries, standardized coinage, and extensive trade networks managed under Arthashastra principles.",
        "The Gupta Era marked a high point for classical Indian art, literature, and science, supported by prosperous inland and oceanic trade routes.",
        "Mughal economic stabilization through land revenue reforms directly funded unprecedented grand architectural and artistic achievements."
      ],
